Using direct property lookup on 'pulseWorkerActionCommands' with a user-controlled parameter 'action' is vulnerable to prototype pollution/lookup issues. For example, if 'action' is 'toString', it will return Function.prototype.toString instead of undefined, which subsequently causes a crash when attempting to access '.command' or call '.join()'. Use Object.hasOwn to safely verify that the action is an explicitly defined command.

